Subject: [PATCH] Preserve contextual identifiers, macro tokens and parenthesized postfix expressions

Type lookahead consumed interpolation modifier names even when no type followed,
so expressions using a local named sample failed (or dereferenced a null node).
Roll back unsuccessful type lookahead while preserving real modifiers. Escape
sample through the generator's existing reserved-word mapping for GLSL ES.

Parse parenthesized constructors as complete expressions before postfix access,
rather than returning early and skipping swizzles/indexing. Keep casts intact.

Keep whitespace and authored parentheses in macro replacement lists and do not
add expression parentheses around declarations or statements. HLSL #define uses
token replacement; grouping belongs in the authored replacement list. Preserve
identity macros and the existing main-texture alias. No authored presets change.

ProjectM TV fix against v4.1.7 plus patches 0001-0035; not an upstream backport.
Reference: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/direct3dhlsl/dx-graphics-hlsl-appendix-pre-define-2
---
